{
  "why": [
    "The snapshot diff of two CONFIGURED captures, read by both languages",
    "(F44-064 a). Go's verify.Differences (what `culprit verify` compares, through",
    "the divergence engine's env_vs_env comparison) and Python's",
    "capture_diff.diff_captures (GET /captures/diff) answer one question: which",
    "(subject, predicate) the two captures answer differently, a key present in",
    "one and not the other included. capture_diff.py's own docstring says a diff",
    "that disagreed with the CLI's about the same two captures would be worse",
    "than none; this file is what holds them to it.",
    "",
    "Each case gives the facts of capture a and capture b (only the fields a",
    "diff reads) and every (subject, predicate) that differs, sorted. Shapes",
    "compare by the shape fixture's equivalence: a length class only as",
    "empty-or-not."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "the same captures",
      "a": [
        {
          "subject": "config:orders/PORT",
          "predicate": "exists",
          "value": true
        },
        {
          "subject": "config:orders/PORT",
          "predicate": "value_shape",
          "value_shape": {
            "type": "string",
            "length_class": "short",
            "format": "numeric",
            "present": true,
            "scheme": "not_applicable"
          }
        }
      ],
      "b": [
